! BINARY VFL INDICATOR SWEEP: M+ / M+MG / M+1 / M-1 LOST CARRY AND
! PARTIAL FIELD, *+ LOST CARRY, LCV AND LTRCV DATA FLAGS, PARTIAL FIELD AND
! TRANSIT WIDTH -- docs/NEXT.md G2.3, the sweep of 2026-11-16.
!
! Every expected value below is HAND-DERIVED from the Reference Manual
! 22-6530-2 (printed N = PDF N+3), read in the page images; none was taken
! from a run.  The capture is vfl_binary_add_indicators.strap's: Z, $IND
! before the operation, the indicator register copied with TI (count one)
! after it; a to-memory case is read back in place, a to-accumulator case
! stores $L and $R, a transit case copies $TR.  Indicator word bits (bit n
! is 1 << (63-n)): LC 0x20000000000, PF 0x10000000000, TF 0x10000000, UF
! 0x8000000, VF 0x4000000, XCZ 0x8000, XVGZ 0x1000, MOP 0x100, RLZ 0x80,
! RZ 0x40, RGZ 0x20, RN 0x10.  A signed binary field at byte size 8 ends in
! an eight-bit sign byte: sign bit 0x08, data flags T U V 0x04 0x02 0x01.
! LC and PF are permanent indicators (printed p.58: "The general result
! exception and the transit indicators are permanent.  If they are turned
! on by any operation, they will remain on until they are turned off either
! by causing an interruption or by being explicitly made zero"), hence the
! Z before every case.
!
! THE RULES:
!  M+ family, LC, printed p.59 (PDF 62): "In binary to-memory operations,
!      this indicator is actuated by a carry beyond the leftmost bit of the
!      addressed field ... This indicator is also actuated when a to-memory
!      operation with an unsigned storage operand produces a negative
!      result.  In all cases, the operation is completed normally except
!      for the loss of the carry."  printed p.62 (M+): "This indicator is
!      also turned on if the result of an unsigned operation is negative.
!      In such a case, the magnitude of the result is stored in storage."
!  M+ family, PF, printed p.59: "In binary operations to storage, this
!      indicator is turned on if there is any one-bit in the accumulator to
!      the left of the participating field."  p.62's Programming Note: the
!      accumulator field is the storage operand's length ("lengthened for
!      the operation by the addition of high-order zeros"), so the bits to
!      its left do not take part in the sum.
!  M+MG: "Lost Carry (LC); Partial Field (PF) ... set as in ADD TO MEMORY"
!      (p.62); "Arithmetic Result ... according to the final result stored".
!  M+1: "Lost Carry (LC) ... These indicators operate as in ADD TO MEMORY"
!      and "identical to an ADD TO MEMORY in which the accumulator operand
!      is +1, except that the partial field indicator is not affected"
!      (p.63); negative sign modifier "a minus one is added" (M-1).
!  Figure 13 (p.62), "Add to Memory, U": storage 3+, accumulator 5- gives
!      "2+*", the star being "The Lost Carry indicator is turned on".
!  *+, printed p.69: "Lost Carry (LC).  In a binary operation, this
!      indicator is set as in ADD"; PF "if the offset is such that
!      significant bits of the product attempt to combine with accumulator
!      positions to the left of the left end of the accumulator".  ADD
!      (p.60): "A partial field condition will not cause a lost carry
!      indication.  However, both conditions may arise".
!  LCV, printed p.73: "Data Flags (TF, UF, VF); To-Memory Operation (MOP);
!      Arithmetic Result (RLZ, RZ, RGZ, RN).  These indicators are set as in
!      ADD"; p.72: "these indicators are set according to the data flag
!      bits, if any, of the storage operand.  Any operation that normally
!      affects these indicators will turn them off if the unsigned modifier
!      is designated."  PF (p.73): "actuated when significant bits of the
!      converted field extend beyond the left end of the accumulator" --
!      no radix in that sentence.
!  LTRCV, printed p.73: data flags "set as in ADD"; PF "if the result of a
!      decimal to binary conversion exceeds 48 significant bits ... only the
!      48 low-order bits of the result are placed in the transit register.
!      This indicator is also actuated if the storage field specified in a
!      decimal-to-binary conversion exceeds 15 decimal digits"; Arithmetic
!      Result "according to the final result in the transit register".
!
! THE CASES (the batch10 model's value, where it differs, in brackets):
!  M1  M+(BU,8,8): acc 1, field FF: 256, the carry leaves the field: 00.
!      LC MOP RZ 0x20000000140.  RZ is the field's sum, CHOSEN (StretchALU's
!      binMemAdd header).                                        [0x120]
!  M2  M+(BU,8,8): acc 1, field FE: FF.  MOP RGZ 0x120.  CONTROL.
!  M3  Figure 13, Add to Memory U, storage 3+ acc 5-: 3 + -5 = -2, the
!      magnitude stored: 02.  LC MOP RLZ RN 0x20000000190.        [0x190]
!  M4  M+MG(BU,8,8): acc -1 (magnitude 1), field FF: 00.  LC MOP RZ
!      0x20000000140.                                             [0x120]
!  M5  M+(BU,8,8): acc (16)102, field 03: the participating 8 bits are 02,
!      bit 8 is a one to their left: 05.  PF MOP RGZ 0x10000000120. [0x120]
!  M6  M+(BU,8,8): acc -(16)102, field 05: 5 + -2 = 3: 03.  PF MOP RGZ
!      0x10000000120.  The batch10 model subtracted all of (16)102: 5 - 258
!      = -253, field FD, 0x190.                          [FD, 0x190]
!  M7  M+1(BU,8): acc (16)102 (PF "not affected"), field FF: 00.  LC MOP RZ
!      0x20000000140, PF off.                                     [0x120]
!  M8  M-1(BU,8): field 00: -1, unsigned, magnitude stored: 01.  LC MOP RLZ
!      RN 0x20000000190.                                          [0x190]
!  M9  M+(B,16,8): acc +5, field -3 (0308): +2, sign byte 00: 0200.  MOP
!      RGZ 0x120.  CONTROL: unlike signs, no LC.
!  M10 M+(B,16,8): acc +1, field +255 (FF00): 256, numeric part 00, sign
!      byte 00: 0000.  LC MOP RZ 0x20000000140.                   [0x120]
!  M11 M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8) with a refill (count 1): the second write site.
!      acc 1, field FF: 00.  LC MOP RZ, and the index result indicators of
!      the pre-refill word (count 0: XCZ; value W11, positive: XVGZ):
!      0x20000009140.  printed p.21 (PDF 24), read in the page image: "The
!      index flag and index result indicators are set following each
!      progressive index operation.  They are set according to the new
!      contents of the index register specified by I.  The setting occurs
!      prior to the refill operation which may be specified."  The address
!      part, 0, is added to the value: W11 stays.                                          [0x9120]
!  P1  *+(BU,8,8): FT 1, multiplier 1, acc 2^128 - 1 (all ones): the carry
!      leaves the left end; acc 0.  LC RZ 0x20000000040.            [0x40]
!  P2  *+: FT -1, multiplier 1, acc all ones: unlike signs, 2^128 - 2.  RGZ
!      0x20.  CONTROL.
!  P3  *+ at offset 120: FT (16)0101, multiplier 1, acc all ones: (16)01
!      past the left end (PF), (16)01 at bit 120 carries out (LC); acc
!      2^120 - 1.  LC PF RGZ 0x30000000020.               [0x10000000020]
!  P4  *+ at offset 120: FT (16)0100, multiplier 1, acc 0: the 1 dropped,
!      0 lands; acc 0.  PF RZ 0x10000000040, LC off.  CONTROL ("will not
!      cause a lost carry indication").
!  C1  LCV(B,16,8) of 050F (5, minus, T U V): acc 5 (BCD), sign byte minus
!      with its flags cleared (p.72).  TF UF VF RLZ RN 0x1C000090.  [0x90]
!  C2  L(B,16,8) of 050F (sets T U V), then LCV(BU,16,8) of it: 1295, BCD
!      (16)1295.  The flags OFF: RGZ 0x20.                   [0x1C000020]
!  C3  LCV(DU,8,4) of 99 at offset 125: 99 = (16)63, bits 125-127 hold 011,
!      the rest past the left end: accL (16)6000000000000000.  PF RGZ
!      0x10000000020.                                              [0x20]
!  C4  the same at offset 120: accL (16)6300000000000000.  RGZ 0x20.
!      CONTROL.
!  C5  LTRCV(DU,64,4) of sixteen digits 000...01: value 1, but the field
!      exceeds 15 digits.  $TR (16)10.  PF RGZ 0x10000000020.      [0x20]
!  C6  LTRCV(DU,60,4) of fifteen nines: 10^15 - 1 = (16)38D7EA4C67FFF, 50
!      bits; the low 48 go to $TR above its four-bit sign byte: $TR
!      (16)8D7EA4C67FFF0.  PF RGZ 0x10000000020.  [$TR (16)38D7EA4C67FFF0]
!  C7  LTRCV(B,16,8) of 050F: $TR (16)58 (5, sign bit 0x08).  TF UF VF RLZ
!      RN 0x1C000090.                                              [0x90]
!  C8  LTRCV(BU,64,8) of 10^15 = (16)38D7EA4C68000: sixteen digits, "In the
!      former case the result is placed in the transit register up to its
!      left end" -- fifteen digits, all zero: $TR 0.  PF, and RZ: the result
!      indicators read "the final result in the transit register".  PF RZ
!      0x10000000040.                                   [0x10000000020]
!
! MEASURED 2026-11-16.  The UNMODIFIED model (batch10) FAILS M1, M3, M4,
! M5, M6 (field and indicators), M7, M8, M10, M11, P1, P3, C1, C2, C3, C5,
! C6 ($TR), C7 -- exactly the bracketed values -- and passes every control
! and every other check.  The fixed model passes all 52 checks and the PC.
! C8, added after the first measurement: batch10 FAILS C8's indicators
! (0x10000000020) and passes its $TR (0), as bracketed.
! INJECTIONS into the fixed model, each in its own scratch copy of the tree
! (the worktree never held one), each run on this deck,
! vfl_binary_add_indicators, vfl_progressive_refill_once and
! vfl_load_factor; the other three decks stayed green unless named:
!   j1 binMemAdd's LC without the field carry (unsigned-negative only):
!      FAILS M1, M4, M7, M10 (0x140), M11 (0x9140).
!   j2 binMemAdd's LC without the unsigned-negative term: FAILS M3, M8
!      (0x190).
!   j3 binMemAdd never sets PF: FAILS M5, M6 (0x120).
!   j4 the accumulator operand NOT masked to the field: FAILS M5
!      (0x30000000120 -- the bit above the field is taken as a carry), M6
!      (field FD, 0x30000000190).
!   j5 M+1 allowed PF (the !addOne guard dropped): NOTHING FAILS.  M+1's
!      addend is the constant 1, so it can never have a bit above the
!      field; the guard is redundant and M7 shows it, not the guard.
!   j6 *+ ignores binAccAdd's LC: FAILS P1 (0x40), P3 (0x10000000020).
!   j7 LCV sets no data flags: FAILS C1 (0x90), C2 (0x1C000020).
!   j8 LTRCV without the fifteen-digit PF: FAILS C5 (0x20).
!   j9 LTRCV keeps sixty bits: FAILS C6 ($TR (16)38D7EA4C67FFF0).
!   j10 decimal LCV without the left-end PF: FAILS C3 (0x20).
! (LTRCV's data flag line was not injected separately; C7 is its check.)
!   j11 binary-to-decimal LTRCV's result indicators read the unmasked
!      result: FAILS C8 (0x10000000020) only.

        SLC, 1000.0
START   L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W1
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W2
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        L(B,16,8), N5
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W3
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        L(B,16,8), N1
        Z, $IND
        M+MG(BU,8,8), W4
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        L(BU,16,8), H0102
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W5
        TI, 1, $IND, I5
        L(B,24,8), N258
        Z, $IND
        M+(BU,8,8), W6
        TI, 1, $IND, I6
        L(BU,16,8), H0102
        Z, $IND
        M+1(BU,8), W7
        TI, 1, $IND, I7
        Z, $IND
        M-1(BU,8), W8
        TI, 1, $IND, I8
        L(BU,8,8), FIVE
        Z, $IND
        M+(B,16,8), W9
        TI, 1, $IND, I9
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        M+(B,16,8), W10
        TI, 1, $IND, I10
        L(BU,8,8), ONE
        LX,  $X7, XPM
        Z, $IND
        M+(V+ICR)(BU,8,8), 0($X7), 0
        TI, 1, $IND, I11
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        LFT(BU,8,8), ONE
        Z, $IND
        *+(BU,8,8), ONE
        TI, 1, $IND, J1
        ST(BU,64,8), A1, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), A1+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        LFT(B,16,8), N1
        Z, $IND
        *+(BU,8,8), ONE
        TI, 1, $IND, J2
        ST(BU,64,8), A2, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), A2+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), ONES, 64
        +(BU,64,8), ONES, 0
        LFT(BU,16,8), H0101
        Z, $IND
        *+(BU,8,8), ONE, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, J3
        ST(BU,64,8), A3, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), A3+1.0
        L(BU,8,8), ZERO
        LFT(BU,16,8), H0100
        Z, $IND
        *+(BU,8,8), ONE, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, J4
        ST(BU,64,8), A4, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), A4+1.0
        Z, $IND
        LCV(B,16,8), FL5
        TI, 1, $IND, K1
        ST(BU,64,8), C1+1.0
        L(BU,64,8), $SB
        ST(BU,64,8), C1+2.0
        Z, $IND
        L(B,16,8), FL5
        LCV(BU,16,8), FL5
        TI, 1, $IND, K2
        ST(BU,64,8), C2+1.0
        Z, $IND
        LCV(DU,8,4), D99, 125
        TI, 1, $IND, K3
        ST(BU,64,8), C3, 64
        ST(BU,64,8), C3+1.0
        Z, $IND
        LCV(DU,8,4), D99, 120
        TI, 1, $IND, K4
        ST(BU,64,8), C4, 64
        Z, $IND
        LTRCV(DU,64,4), D16
        TI, 1, $IND, K5
        TI, 1, $TR, T5
        Z, $IND
        LTRCV(DU,60,4), D15N
        TI, 1, $IND, K6
        TI, 1, $TR, T6
        Z, $IND
        LTRCV(B,16,8), FL5
        TI, 1, $IND, K7
        TI, 1, $TR, T7
        Z, $IND
        LTRCV(BU,64,8), B15
        TI, 1, $IND, K8
        TI, 1, $TR, T8
PASS    BEW, $


        SLC, 1500.0
XPM     XW, W11, 1, RFW          ! count 1: the refill fires
RFW     XW, 1234.0, 77, 1500.0   ! the refilled index word
N5      DD(BU,64), (16)0508000000000000
N1      DD(BU,64), (16)0108000000000000
